# The image is one Go binary, so the context is hub/ and nothing else.
#
# Written as "exclude everything, then add back" rather than as a list of
# exclusions: the hub is now the only thing that gets built here, and a new
# top-level directory should not silently start bloating the context or busting
# the layer cache.
*
!hub/

# Inside hub/, the build reads the module files, the Go source, and the built
# console that embed.go carries into the binary. The rest is either build-time
# tooling or already compiled into dist/.
#
# node_modules is ~200MB that never reaches the image; the console's TypeScript
# is already built; the Playwright suite needs a running hub and a browser, so
# it could not run in here anyway.
hub/web/node_modules/
hub/web/src/
hub/web/e2e/
hub/web/public/
hub/web/test-results/
hub/web/playwright-report/
hub/web/package.json
hub/web/package-lock.json
hub/web/*.config.*
hub/web/tsconfig*.json
hub/web/index.html

# Go tests do not run in the image build - CI runs them, with -race, which needs
# a toolchain this stage deliberately does not have.
hub/**/*_test.go
hub/**/testdata/

# Local state that must never reach a layer.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
